From 5577f1f3f066d25571864c94b90e5e7b38be5fe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:15:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bump the widget cache buster so browsers pick up the renamed
 widget

The loader requests /widget/rito.js?v=texto-1 and the response carries
cache-control: public, max-age=3600, so a returning visitor keeps the
old widget for up to an hour after the rename ships and still sees the
name Rito.

Measured against production: a request with a never-before-used query
string came back x-vercel-cache: HIT with the same age as the canonical
URL, so the CDN is not keyed on the query string and this bump does
nothing there. It only busts the browser cache, which is keyed on the
full URL.

That is why this is a separate commit. Shipping it together with the
rename races the two deployments: the static site could publish a
loader asking for v=rita-1 before the agents project publishes the new
widget, and browsers would cache the old file under the new key for an
hour. Apply this only after the agents deployment already serves Rita.
---
 rito-loader.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rito-loader.js b/rito-loader.js
index c1ce5eb..e2e07fa 100644
--- a/rito-loader.js
+++ b/rito-loader.js
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
     'https://retirobtc-agents.vercel.app';
   var base = url.replace(/\/$/, '');
   var s = document.createElement('script');
-  s.src = base + '/widget/rito.js?v=texto-1';
+  s.src = base + '/widget/rito.js?v=rita-1';
   s.setAttribute('data-agents-url', base);
   s.defer = true;
   s.onerror = function () {
